1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,920
Still exhausted, foggy, and stuck at the same weight even though you take your thyroid pill every single morning?

2
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:07,105
It might not be your dose that's the problem.

3
00:00:07,425 --> 00:00:12,285
Levothyroxine needs an empty stomach and a clear runway to actually get absorbed into your bloodstream.

4
00:00:12,605 --> 00:00:20,641
A handful of everyday foods and drinks can bind to it or block it before your body ever gets the full dose - coffee, soy, and walnuts are the three biggest offenders.

5
00:00:20,961 --> 00:00:22,657
Coffee is one of the most common ones.

6
00:00:22,977 --> 00:00:30,448
Even a small cup taken too close to your pill can cut how much of your dose actually gets absorbed by up to 30%, according to research on the interaction.

7
00:00:30,768 --> 00:00:39,405
Try waiting at least 30 to 60 minutes after your pill before your first sip - that gap alone lets your body absorb what you actually swallowed.

8
00:00:39,725 --> 00:00:41,000
Soy is the sneaky one.

9
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:48,405
Soy milk, tofu, and other soy products bind to levothyroxine in your gut and block a big chunk of it from ever reaching your bloodstream.

10
00:00:48,725 --> 00:00:55,534
Keep soy at least 4 hours away from your dose - a soy latte right after your pill undoes a lot of what the medication is supposed to do.

11
00:00:55,854 --> 00:00:57,044
Walnuts work the same way.

12
00:00:57,364 --> 00:01:04,125
The fiber and compounds in them bind to the medication and drag your absorption down, whether they're a snack or mixed into breakfast.

13
00:01:04,445 --> 00:01:08,186
Same rule applies - give it 4 hours between your pill and a handful of walnuts.

14
00:01:08,506 --> 00:01:13,642
None of this means giving up coffee, soy, or walnuts for good - it's really just about timing.

15
00:01:13,962 --> 00:01:19,496
Take your pill on an empty stomach first thing, then give it that window before anything else touches your system.
